---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Muscle — The 4M Framework | My4MLife"
  description="Muscle is neuroprotection. Resistance training, hormone optimization, peptides, and body composition are the physical engine of cognitive longevity."
  canonical="https://www.my4mlife.com/pillars/muscle"
  keywords="testosterone therapy, hormone optimization, GLP-1 weight loss, growth hormone peptides, body composition, muscle, cognitive longevity, My4MLife"
  ogImage="https://www.my4mlife.com/og-image.svg"
  robots="index, follow"
>

<!-- ===== HERO ===== -->
<section class="pillar-hero pillar-hero--muscle">
  <div class="pillar-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src="/images/scenes/muscle-active.jpg" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="pillar-hero-overlay"></div>
  </div>
    <div class="container pillar-hero-inner">
    <p class="pillar-kicker">PILLAR 2 OF 4 — MUSCLE</p>
    <h1>Muscle</h1>
    <p class="pillar-tagline"><em>Strong body, sharp mind. Resistance training is neuroprotection.</em></p>
    <p class="pillar-value">
      Muscle is not vanity. Lean muscle mass is one of the strongest predictors of all-cause mortality and cognitive healthspan. Sarcopenia — the loss of skeletal muscle with age — drives metabolic decline, hormonal dysfunction, and cognitive deterioration simultaneously.
    </p>
    <p class="pillar-value">
      The Muscle pillar is broader than weight loss. It is the comprehensive body-engine pillar: hormones, peptides, body composition, pain management, and the exercise and nutrition protocols that tie it all together.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== FRAMEWORK ROLE ===== -->
<section class="pillar-section pillar-section--light">
  <div class="container pillar-prose">
    <h2>The Role of Muscle in the 4M Framework</h2>
    <p>
      Resistance training is the most well-documented behavioral intervention for cognitive longevity outside of sleep. It upregulates BDNF (brain-derived neurotrophic factor), the primary growth factor for neurons. It improves insulin sensitivity — a key driver of neuroinflammation when dysregulated. It preserves lean mass, which directly correlates with metabolic health and hormonal balance through the fifth, sixth, and seventh decades of life.
    </p>
    <p>
      But training in a hormonal deficit is like building on sand. Testosterone and growth hormone optimize the tissue response to exercise. Peptide protocols accelerate recovery, body composition, and cellular repair. GLP-1 therapy addresses visceral adiposity — a direct neurotoxin when elevated chronically. Pain that limits activity, whether acute or chronic, is a direct threat to this pillar and must be addressed as part of the protocol. The Muscle pillar coordinates all of these levers so that the body becomes — and stays — the physical engine the brain requires.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== SUB-TOPICS ===== -->
<section class="pillar-section">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Sub-Topics Under the Muscle Pillar</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Six focus areas — from hormone optimization to pain management and everything between.</p>
    <div class="subtopic-grid">

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>Testosterone Therapy &amp; Hormone Optimization</h3>
        <p>Testosterone replacement therapy and men's hormone optimization — TRT protocols, lab-guided dosing, and the downstream effects on muscle, cognition, mood, and libido.</p>
        <a href="/solutions/hormones" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>Growth Hormone Peptides</h3>
        <p>Sermorelin, CJC-1295/Ipamorelin, Tesamorelin, and MK-677 — growth hormone secretagogues that optimize body composition, recovery, and sleep architecture without exogenous HGH.</p>
        <a href="/solutions/peptides" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>GLP-1 Weight Loss &amp; Body Composition</h3>
        <p>Semaglutide and tirzepatide for visceral adiposity reduction — available through the comprehensive 4M consult pathway. Body composition is brain health.</p>
        <a href="/solutions/weight" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>Acute Pain Limiting Activity</h3>
        <p>Injury, post-surgical limitation, or acute musculoskeletal pain that disrupts training continuity — addressed directly so exercise compliance doesn't collapse.</p>
        <a href="/solutions/pain-acute" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>Chronic Pain Management</h3>
        <p>Long-standing pain conditions that create a sedentary trap — fibromyalgia, degenerative joint disease, chronic back pain. Protocol-based management to restore function.</p>
        <a href="/solutions/pain-chronic" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card">
        <h3>Exercise Protocols &amp; Nutrition</h3>
        <p>Progressive overload programming, nutrition periodization, and daily movement tracking — the foundational layer delivered weekly through the My4MLife App at every tier.</p>
        <a href="/membership" class="explore-link">Explore &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <div class="subtopic-card subtopic-card--rpa">
        <div class="rpa-pill">REGENERATIVE TIER</div>
        <h3>Regenerative Medicine — Solutions for Chronic Pain &amp; Joint Degeneration</h3>
        <p>When chronic pain or joint degeneration doesn't respond to PT, NSAIDs, anti-inflammatory protocols, or peptides — regenerative medicine solutions coordinated through our partner regenerative medicine practice may help. Nationwide mobile delivery.</p>
        <a href="/regenerative-medicine" class="explore-link">Learn About Regenerative Medicine Solutions &rarr;</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== IN DEVELOPMENT: NEUROLIFT ===== -->
<section class="pillar-section pillar-section--light">
  <div class="container pillar-prose">
    <aside class="research-callout">
      <h3>What the research actually says — creatine for muscle</h3>
      <p class="research-callout-intro">There is no second-best ergogenic supplement. The International Society of Sports Nutrition explicitly designates creatine monohydrate as the gold standard — and the meta-analysis on creatine for sarcopenia is the strongest published evidence for any lifestyle intervention against age-related muscle loss.</p>
      <ul class="research-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Creatine monohydrate is "the most effective ergogenic nutritional supplement currently available to athletes."</strong> Position stand authored by 30 contributing researchers; the consensus document in the field. 30+ years of safety data. <span class="research-source">Kreider et al., <em>Journal of the International Society of Sports Nutrition</em>, 2017. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28615996/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed 28615996</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Creatine + resistance training in older adults: +1.4 kg additional lean mass, +9.5 kg chest press, +14 kg leg press</strong> above resistance training alone. Meta-analysis of 22 RCTs. This is the single strongest published evidence base for any sarcopenia mitigation strategy. <span class="research-source">Chilibeck et al., <em>Open Access Journal of Sports Medicine</em>, 2017. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29138605/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed 29138605</a>.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>8g L-citrulline malate one hour before training increased reps performed by 52.9%</strong> and reduced 24-hour muscle soreness by 40%. The NO blend doesn't just support sexual performance — it's a direct ergogenic in the gym. <span class="research-source">Pérez-Guisado &amp; Jakeman, <em>Journal of Strength and Conditioning Research</em>, 2010. <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20386132/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed 20386132</a>.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="research-callout-footnote"><em>This isn't a debate. The evidence stack behind creatine + L-citrulline + beetroot is broader and more replicated than anything else in the sports nutrition category. We just package it for the cognitive longevity audience instead of the gym-bro audience.</em></p>
    </aside>

    <aside class="product-in-dev">
      <span class="product-in-dev-badge">In development — Q4 2026</span>
      <h3>MitoVita — one mechanism, four outcomes</h3>
      <p class="product-in-dev-tagline">The mitochondrial supplement that bridges Mind, Muscle, and Mitigate.</p>
      <p>Creatine monohydrate (5g) + L-citrulline malate (6g) + standardized beetroot extract + functional electrolyte matrix. Once daily, fast-compatible, monk-fruit sweetened. Designed for split-dose pre/post fasted workout use — half before, half after, then break the fast with 30g+ lean protein.</p>
      <p>Mitochondria are the upstream node behind every age-related decline in our demographic — cognitive function, sarcopenia, visceral-fat metabolism, and sexual performance all trace to mitochondrial ATP capacity under adequate vascular supply. Creatine buffers mitochondrial ATP. L-citrulline and beetroot drive nitric oxide production, dilating the vessels that deliver oxygen to those mitochondria. One mechanism. Four outcomes. (Magnesium is intentionally separated — it lives in the existing SleepRestore formula, timed for evening sleep-architecture support, not daytime performance.)</p>
      <p>The Muscle pillar isn't vanity. Lean muscle drives insulin sensitivity, reduces visceral adiposity, lowers the inflammatory cytokine load crossing the blood-brain barrier, and protects the metabolic flexibility that determines healthspan.</p>
      <p class="product-in-dev-note">Formulation under clinical advisory board review. See the cognitive solution page and the erectile-dysfunction page for the full mind-side and vascular-side rationale.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== APP DELIVERY ===== -->
<section class="pillar-section pillar-section--dark">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>How the My4MLife App Delivers the Muscle Pillar</h2>
    <p class="app-intro">Exercise protocols and nutrition guidance are a core deliverable of the My4MLife program — structured by tier, progressive by month.</p>
    <div class="tier-delivery-grid">
      <div class="tier-delivery-card">
        <div class="tier-badge tier-badge--free">Protégé — Free</div>
        <p>Foundational baseline: Month 1 resistance training framework, daily movement tracker, introductory nutrition principles. All within the My4MLife App — no card required.</p>
        <a href="/membership" class="tier-link">Start free &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-delivery-card">
        <div class="tier-badge tier-badge--insider">Insider+</div>
        <p>Advanced progressive overload programming, nutrition periodization (month-by-month), supplement guidance, and body composition tracking. Monthly Q&amp;A with Dr. TJ on Muscle pillar questions.</p>
        <a href="/membership" class="tier-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-delivery-card">
        <div class="tier-badge tier-badge--grad">Graduate</div>
        <p>Lifetime protocol library including member-only resources, peptide candidacy review, hormone panel interpretation, and personal body-composition protocol design with Dr. TJ.</p>
        <a href="/membership" class="tier-link">Learn more &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== CTAs ===== -->
<section class="pillar-section pillar-cta-section">
  <div class="container pillar-cta-inner">
    <h2>Your Solution Path</h2>
    <div class="cta-chain">
      <a href="/assessment" class="cta-btn cta-btn--primary">Take the Free Assessment &rarr;</a>
      <a href="https://app.my4mlife.com" class="cta-btn cta-btn--outline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download the My4MLife App — Free &rarr;</a>
      <a href="/consult" class="cta-btn cta-btn--outline">Schedule a Comprehensive 4M Consult &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===== DISCLAIMER ===== -->
<section class="pillar-disclaimer">
  <div class="container">
    <p>My4MLife is a lifestyle and wellness education platform. Content on this page is for informational purposes only and does not constitute medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. All clinical services, including Rx protocols and telemedicine consultations, are delivered by a separately contracted, fully licensed telemedicine practice operating under its own professional obligations. Results vary. Always consult a qualified healthcare provider before beginning any new health protocol.</p>
  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.pillar-hero {
  padding: 9rem 0 6rem;
  text-align: center;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.pillar-hero-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; }
.pillar-hero-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
.pillar-hero-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(160deg, rgba(10,22,40,0.88) 0%, rgba(26,58,92,0.78) 50%, rgba(15,76,117,0.85) 100%); }
.pillar-hero--muscle {
  background: linear-gradient(160deg, #0a1628 0%, #1a3a5c 50%, #0f4c75 100%);
}
.pillar-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
.pillar-kicker {
  font-size: 0.72rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 2px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent);
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.pillar-hero h1 {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 4rem;
  color: white;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.pillar-tagline {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8);
  margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
}
.pillar-value {
  font-size: 1.05rem;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
  max-width: 680px;
  margin: 0 auto 1.2rem;
  line-height: 1.8;
}
.pillar-section { padding: 5.5rem 0; }
.pillar-section--light { background: var(--bg-soft); }
.pillar-section--dark {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0a1628 0%, #0f4c75 100%);
}
.pillar-prose h2,
.pillar-section h2 {
  font-size: 2rem;
  margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  color: var(--dark);
}
.pillar-section--dark h2 { color: white; }
.pillar-prose p { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.8; }
.section-sub { color: var(--text-light); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
.subtopic-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 1.5rem;
}
.subtopic-card {
  background: white;
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: 1.8rem 1.5rem;
  transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;
}
.subtopic-card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-3px);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  border-color: var(--accent);
}
.subtopic-card h3 {
  font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
  font-size: 1.1rem;
  color: var(--primary);
  margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
}
.subtopic-card p {
  font-size: 0.88rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
  line-height: 1.65;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
}
.explore-link {
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  color: var(--accent);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.explore-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.app-intro {
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
  font-size: 1rem;
  margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  max-width: 600px;
}
.tier-delivery-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: 1.5rem;
}
.tier-delivery-card {
  background: rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: 1.8rem;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.tier-delivery-card p {
  font-size: 0.88rem;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65);
  line-height: 1.7;
  flex: 1;
}
.tier-badge {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 1.5px;
  padding: 0.3rem 0.8rem;
  border-radius: 20px;
  width: fit-content;
}
.tier-badge--free { background: rgba(0,184,148,0.15); color: var(--accent); }
.tier-badge--insider { background: rgba(226,184,74,0.15); color: #e2b84a; }
.tier-badge--grad { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); }
.tier-link {
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  color: var(--accent);
  text-decoration: none;
}
.tier-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
.pillar-cta-section { background: var(--bg-soft); text-align: center; }
.pillar-cta-inner h2 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
.cta-chain {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 1rem;
}
.cta-btn {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 0.85rem 2rem;
  border-radius: 50px;
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  font-weight: 600;
  text-decoration: none;
  transition: all 0.25s;
}
.cta-btn--primary { background: var(--accent); color: white; }
.cta-btn--primary:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); transform: translateY(-1px); box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,184,148,0.4); }
.cta-btn--outline { background: transparent; color: var(--primary); border: 2px solid var(--primary); }
.cta-btn--outline:hover { background: var(--primary); color: white; }
.pillar-disclaimer {
  background: #f7fafc;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  padding: 2rem 0;
}
.pillar-disclaimer p {
  font-size: 0.75rem;
  color: var(--text-light);
  line-height: 1.7;
  max-width: 880px;
}
.subtopic-card--rpa {
  border-color: rgba(0,184,148,0.4);
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(0,184,148,0.04) 0%, rgba(15,76,117,0.04) 100%);
  position: relative;
}
.subtopic-card--rpa:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
.rpa-pill {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 0.65rem;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 1.5px;
  color: var(--accent);
  background: rgba(0,184,148,0.12);
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,184,148,0.4);
  padding: 0.2rem 0.7rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .subtopic-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
  .tier-delivery-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 440px; margin: 0 auto; }
}
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .pillar-hero { padding: 7rem 0 4rem; }
  .pillar-hero h1 { font-size: 2.8rem; }
  .subtopic-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}
</style>
